.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-peakformant 1  "pvc-peakformant " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-peakformant \- Peak formant tracker: a time\-series of the loudest bin\*(Aqs frequency over a detection band, never audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-peakformant\fR [\fB\-\-fft\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-octave\-pitchclass\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-channel\-method\fR] [\fB\-\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-warp\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-reference\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-type\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Peak formant tracker: a time\-series of the loudest bin\*(Aqs frequency over a detection band, never audio.
.PP
Ports `peakformant`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/ peakformant.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::peakformant`\*(Aqs doc comment for why it reuses `pvc centroid`\*(Aqs whole two\-pass pipeline (confirmed byte\-for\-byte identical apart from the one real per\-frame analysis difference).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fft\fR \fI<FFT>\fR [default: 1024]

.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 2048]

.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]

.TP
\fB\-\-band\-octave\-pitchclass\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-band\-low\fR \fI<BAND_LOW>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-band\-high\fR \fI<BAND_HIGH>\fR [default: \-1]
`< 0` means Nyquist
.TP
\fB\-\-channel\-method\fR \fI<CHANNEL_METHOD>\fR [default: average]

.TP
\fB\-\-attack\fR \fI<ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
`\-l`: envelope ascent (attack) time
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-L`: envelope descent (release) time
.TP
\fB\-\-warp\fR \fI<WARP>\fR [default: 0]

.TP
\fB\-\-output\-rate\fR \fI<OUTPUT_RATE>\fR [default: 500]

.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR [default: freq]

.TP
\fB\-\-reference\-pitch\fR \fI<REFERENCE_PITCH>\fR [default: 8]
Reference pitch in octave.pitchclass notation, used only by `semitones\-deviation`/`neg\-semitones\-deviation` output formats
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-type\fR \fI<OUTPUT_TYPE>\fR [default: ascii]

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

